# parts.zd — a post that names a component (issue #305).
#
# `writing.zd` reads `content/*.md` and renders each file as one `Prose`.
# That is every post this language could publish until now, and it is the
# one thing the MDX pipeline does that it could not: **a post could not
# name a component.** The day a post wants an interactive chart, the chart
# has to come from somewhere the markdown cannot reach.
#
# ## Why `Prose` could not simply grow children
#
# `Prose` has no children, and the reason is in `elements.rs`: interleaving
# parsed nodes with templated ones would make the sibling offsets every
# binding is scheduled against depend on how many nodes a *file* parsed
# into, which is not known at compile time. That argument is sound and it
# does not go away, so the answer is not an escape hatch inside the markup.
#
# ## The shape that works
#
# A post stops being one `Markup` and becomes a **list of parts**. Each
# part is either a run of prose or a named widget, the document is an
# ordinary `each` over that list, and each part is its own node — so no
# parsed subtree ever shares a parent with a templated one and the offset
# problem never arises.
#
# ## The widget set is closed, and the program owns it
#
# A component cannot be resolved from a file's text: components are
# resolved statically and a name out of a `.md` is not a name the compiler
# saw. So the *program* declares which widgets a post may use, and a post
# naming anything else is a **failed build** — not a blank space. That is a
# stronger bargain than MDX makes, where an `import` inside a content file
# can reach anything on disk.
#
# Try it: change `spacetrader-wars.md` to say ```zd PieChart``` and the
# build stops, naming the widget and listing the two this program offers.

# The closed set. Its variants are the whole of what a document under
# `content/parts/` may name, and the compiler reads them: `build parts`
# refuses a name that is not one of these at the moment the file is read.
choice Widget
    RingChart
    StackBars

record Post
    slug is Text
    # `List of Part`, where `writing.zd` has one `Markup`. `Part` is a
    # prelude record and `build parts` is the only thing that makes one.
    parts is List of Part

state posts is static List of Post from readPosts with directory is "content/parts"

function readPosts with directory
    from build list directory
    map each path to postFrom with path

function postFrom with path
    give Post with slug is path, parts is build parts (build read path)

# The two widgets, as ordinary components. Nothing about them is special:
# they hold `client` state, they respond to clicks, and they would be
# written exactly this way if the page had named them itself. What the
# capability adds is that a *file* may ask for one.
component RingChart with argument
    state share is client Whole starting 60

    Column padding is 8
        Text argument
        Meter share, least is 0, most is 100, low is 20, high is 80, best is 60, label is "share"
        Row
            Button "less"
                on click
                    subtract 10 from share
            Button "more"
                on click
                    add 10 to share

component StackBars with argument
    state open is client Truth starting no

    Column padding is 8
        Text argument
        Button "show the second bar"
            on click
                set open to not open
        if open
            Text "the second bar"

# The dispatch, and the one place this program spells the names twice.
#
# The `choice` above is the declaration; this is the elimination. They are
# two constructs rather than one because the language has no way to turn a
# `Text` into a variant of a `choice` — `when` eliminates a choice value,
# and what arrives here is a name. The compiler holds the two together at
# the only point where being wrong would matter: a name the `choice` does
# not offer never reaches this component, because the build stopped.
component PostWidget with name, argument
    if name is "RingChart"
        RingChart argument
    if name is "StackBars"
        StackBars argument

view title is "A post that names a component"
    Column
        Heading "Posts"

        each post in posts
            Column padding is 8
                Text post.slug

                each part in post.parts
                    # The whole of the dispatch. A record rather than a
                    # `choice` because this one test is all it takes, and a
                    # choice with payloads would need construction and
                    # elimination machinery to earn the distinction.
                    if isBlank of part.widget
                        Prose part.markup
                    if not (isBlank of part.widget)
                        PostWidget part.widget, part.argument
